# Example ReRDMFT input file: LiH, 6-31G, GNOF, FULL_OPTIMIZATION TRUE, with FCIDUMP TRUE --
# writes an FCIDUMP file (Utils/Fcidump.h, the MOLPRO/PySCF convention: "&FCI ... &END" header,
# then one integral per line "VALUE I J K L") of the spin-up channel's one- and two-electron MO
# integrals, in the SAME orbital order FULL_OPTIMIZATION's own rotation left them in -- for
# handing off to an external CI/DMRG/FCI code. NON_RELATIVISTIC only (the only case currently
# supported); requires FUNCTIONAL. Sanity check: summing FCIDUMP's own integrals over the two
# doubly-occupied spatial MOs with the closed-shell RHF energy formula reproduces the SCF-only
# (no FULL_OPTIMIZATION) energy exactly; with FULL_OPTIMIZATION on, the one-electron diagonal
# elements differ from the SCF-only run's own FCIDUMP (confirming the rotation is applied before
# writing, not the raw canonical HF orbitals).
NELEC 4
BASIS lih-6-31g.gbs
NON_RELATIVISTIC TRUE
FUNCTIONAL GNOF
PNOF_SUBSPACES 2
PNOF_COUPLING 2
FULL_OPTIMIZATION TRUE
FCIDUMP TRUE
USE_RI FALSE  # preserve this example's pre-existing dense/Cholesky path (USE_RI now defaults TRUE)

GEOMETRY
Li  0.000000   0.000000   0.000000
H   0.000000   0.000000   1.594900
END
